# Releasing `{{ project_name }}`

{% if is_library -%}
`{{ project_name }}` follows SemVer; in pre-1.0, a minor bump may carry
breaking changes.
{% if release_automation == 'github-oidc' %}
Releases publish automatically via GitHub Actions **Trusted Publishing**
(OIDC: no PyPI token is stored anywhere). Procedure for `X.Y.Z`:

1. Promote `CHANGELOG.md`'s `[Unreleased]` section to `[X.Y.Z]` (see
   `.agents/changelog.md`).
2. Bump `version` in `pyproject.toml`; `uv sync --group dev` to refresh
   `uv.lock`.
3. Commit `🔖 Release version X.Y.Z` (body references the `[X.Y.Z]`
   entry) and push.
4. Tag and push:
   `git tag -a vX.Y.Z -m "🔖 Release version X.Y.Z" && git push origin vX.Y.Z`.

The `v*.*.*` tag triggers `.github/workflows/publish.yml`: it reruns
CI across the OS matrix, builds the distributions once (failing fast
if the tag does not match the `pyproject.toml` version) and uploads
them as an artifact,{% if use_testpypi %} publishes them to TestPyPI as a staging
rehearsal,{% endif %} then, once you approve the `pypi` environment gate,
publishes the same artifacts to PyPI via OIDC. A final `github-release`
job then creates the GitHub Release for the tag automatically, with
the sdist + wheel attached; there is no manual release step. Its notes
are the matching `CHANGELOG.md` section with each wrapped paragraph or
list item joined onto one line (GitHub renders every newline in a
release body as a line break), closed by a `**Full Changelog**` line
taken from the section's link reference. Keeping `build`
separate from publish keeps the `id-token: write` permission scoped
to the publish jobs only.

## One-time setup (before the first release)

1. **PyPI Trusted Publisher**: on PyPI, register a GitHub Actions
   publisher for the project: owner `{{ github_username }}`, repo
   `{{ repo_name }}`, workflow `publish.yml`, environment `pypi`. Use
   PyPI's *pending publisher* form for the very first upload (before
   the project exists on PyPI).
{%- if use_testpypi %}
2. **TestPyPI Trusted Publisher**: register the *same* publisher on
   [test.pypi.org](https://test.pypi.org/manage/account/publishing/)
   for the staging job: owner `{{ github_username }}`, repo
   `{{ repo_name }}`, workflow `publish.yml`. The `testpypi` job has
   no environment, so leave that field blank.
3. **GitHub `pypi` environment**: create an environment named `pypi`
   in the repo settings and add yourself as a *required reviewer*, so
   every publish waits for explicit approval.
{%- else %}
2. **GitHub `pypi` environment**: create an environment named `pypi`
   in the repo settings and add yourself as a *required reviewer*, so
   every publish waits for explicit approval.

If you decide you want a TestPyPI rehearsal step later, re-run
`copier update` with `use_testpypi=true`: the pipeline gains a
`testpypi` job between `build` and `pypi`.
{%- endif %}
{%- else %}
Release procedure for `X.Y.Z`:

1. Promote `CHANGELOG.md`'s `[Unreleased]` section to `[X.Y.Z]` (see
   `.agents/changelog.md`).
2. Bump `version` in `pyproject.toml`; `uv sync --group dev` to
   refresh `uv.lock`.
3. Commit: `🔖 Release version X.Y.Z`, body referencing the new
   `[X.Y.Z]` CHANGELOG entry.
4. `uv build`. Validate with `uvx twine check dist/*` and a fresh
   install in an isolated environment
   (`uv run --isolated --no-project --with dist/*.whl python -c "..."`).
{%- if use_testpypi %}
5. Publish to TestPyPI first:
   `uv publish --index testpypi --username __token__ --keyring-provider subprocess`.
   Verify the project page and a fresh install from
   `test.pypi.org/simple/`.
6. Publish to PyPI with the same command using `--index pypi`.
7. Annotated tag `vX.Y.Z` whose message starts with
   `🔖 Release version X.Y.Z` and references the CHANGELOG; push the
   tag.
{%- else %}
5. Publish to PyPI:
   `uv publish --index pypi --username __token__ --keyring-provider subprocess`.
6. Annotated tag `vX.Y.Z` whose message starts with
   `🔖 Release version X.Y.Z` and references the CHANGELOG; push the
   tag.
{%- endif %}

Tokens live in the OS keyring at the `publish-url` key
(`keyring set <publish-url> __token__`), scoped per-project once the
package exists on the index. {% if use_testpypi %}Named indexes (`pypi`, `testpypi`) are{% else %}The `pypi` named index is{% endif %}
configured under `[[tool.uv.index]]` in `pyproject.toml`.
{%- endif %}
{%- else -%}
`{{ project_name }}` is an application and is not published; a version
marks a notable state of the project. Procedure for `X.Y.Z`:

1. Promote `CHANGELOG.md`'s `[Unreleased]` section to `[X.Y.Z]` (see
   `.agents/changelog.md`).
2. Bump `version` in `pyproject.toml`; `uv sync --group dev` to refresh
   `uv.lock`.
3. Commit `🔖 Release version X.Y.Z` (body references the `[X.Y.Z]`
   entry).
4. Tag and push:
   `git tag -a vX.Y.Z -m "🔖 Release version X.Y.Z" && git push origin vX.Y.Z`.
{%- endif %}
